        allowfullscreen
        sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation allow-popups">
      </iframe>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-5 bg-body-tertiary border-bottom">
  <div class="site-shell">
    <div class="row g-3">
      <div class="col-lg-6">
        <div class="h-100 p-4 p-lg-5 rounded-4 border bg-body">
          <p class="text-uppercase fw-bold small text-primary mb-1">Core argument</p>
          <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-3">Technology alone is not enough</h2>
          <p class="text-muted mb-0">The dissertation's case studies showed that mobile devices do not automatically produce meaningful collaboration, argumentation or knowledge building. What matters for learning is how the activity is designed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-6">
        <div class="row g-3">
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="h-100 p-4 rounded-4 border bg-body">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Mobile devices as cognitive tools</h3>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Devices can support information seeking, documentation, conversation and shared problem-solving when connected to the learning task.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="h-100 p-4 rounded-4 border bg-body">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Collaborative scripts</h3>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Learners need structures that make joint work visible and guide discussion toward knowledge building.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-12">
            <div class="h-100 p-4 rounded-4 border bg-body">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Pedagogical scaffolding</h3>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">The learning process is built through phases where technology, tasks, guidance and interaction support each other.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-5" id="papers">
